WEBVTT

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.440
Today, the student council needs to 
go over plans for the culture fair.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.860
Wait, first we should gather the 
materials from past years...

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.490
What's this?

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.150
Vice President Shinomiya.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.550
Oh, Mutsumi-chan.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.850
What's going on?

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.700
It seems the cafeteria isn't open today.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.080
Huh?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.590
<b>Temporarily Closed
 Today</b>

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.110
Oh, well.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.090
Let's get something at the school store.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:33.840
Wow...

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.180
That's a lot of people.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.420
I wanted to review all the student 
council work while eating lunch, but...

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.670
Why don't you go do your work, Vice President?

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.280
I'll get food for both of us.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.660
Really?

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.360
Oh, that's great.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.560
Could I ask you to get something for me, too?

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.210
President Amatsu.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.110
I'll make some tea and wait for you.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.990
I appreciate it.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.130
<b>Student Council</b>

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.130
That's everything for the student council today.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.670
<b>Darjeeling with Everyone</b>

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:35.890
If there's no objection,

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.840
I'll go submit today's minutes to the vice principal.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.710
Will that be all right, President?

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.290
Hold on a second.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.140
Hm? Is there a problem?

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.050
It looks like the water needs a bit longer to boil.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.890
Could you wait until then?

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.650
Sure.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.900
Here you go.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.570
I got some really good tea today.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.960
It smells like muscat.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.010
It's Darjeeling, second flush,

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.370
supreme muscatel.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.750
The only thing the president 
does well is make good tea.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.890
What?

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.130
The only thing?

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.350
<i>The only thing.</i>

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.360
<i>Yep, the only thing.</i>

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.810
<i>The only thing, yes.</i>

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.520
Good work, everyone.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.500
It looks like your meeting is over.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.030
Vice Principal.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.990
Yes, no problems here.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.640
There are never any problems with 
you at the helm, Shinomiya-san.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.100
You're a great help, Risa-chan.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.690
I have something to tell you all.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.300
The school cafeteria will be closed for a while.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.150
What?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.040
The cafeteria staff were on vacation together

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.880
when bad weather grounded their plane,

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.770
and now it seems they're stuck.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.050
They can't make it back by train?

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:54.480
There aren't any trains where they are.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.300
Where is that?

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.340
Easter Island.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.320
Overseas, huh?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.200
We'll be in real trouble if the 
cafeteria stays closed too long.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.370
The school store was packed, too.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.410
I heard many students

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.100
didn't get to eat anything after 
the school store ran out of stock.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.270
Ask the students to start 
bringing their lunches for now.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.890
Understood.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.530
Does that sound all right, President?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.320
Is something the matter?

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.280
I have a good idea.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.780
Huh?

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.790
How about the student council 
members staff the cafeteria?

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.300
What?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.190
Here we go again...

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.600
I'm sure there are students 
who can't bring a lunch.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.800
I think it'd be great if we could help out.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.080
We can't run a cafeteria on our own.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.020
But you can cook, can't you?

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.240
A little...

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.440
But we'd have to make so much.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.440
We have enough people.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.190
We don't have the experience.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.910
I'm sure if we try...

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.920
Who's going to be trying?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.190
Try your best!

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.520
Jeez.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.880
You always get these ideas 
and make us do the work.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.040
What's impossible is impossible.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.380
It's not completely impossible.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:14.830
Huh?

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.680
Vice Principal...

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.300
I have a nutritionist license,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.340
so I'll direct you.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.480
What?

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.820
The ingredients we ordered have already arrived,

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.920
and the refrigerator is full.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.710
If we don't use them, they'll spoil,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.440
so it might be good to have the student 
council run the cafeteria for a time.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.400
But...

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.070
Sorry, but I'd like all of you to

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:38.100
come in early tomorrow for training.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.980
I appreciate it, everyone.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.320
Stew, curry, meat with potatoes...

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:50.130
We'll focus on items that we 
can make a lot of at once,

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:54.210
and round it out with fried foods, salad, and 
noodles, since they just need to be warmed.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.060
Right!

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:58.210
Okay, split up and start getting everything ready.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.210
Right!

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:04.040
Toudou-sensei, you're really good at this.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.950
This is basic cooking knowledge.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.560
If you're not good with a knife, 
don't force it. Use a peeler.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.220
Okay.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.660
It's a lot of work when there's this much food.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.000
It'll go quickly if we all work together.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.890
Yeah, it doesn't take any special techniques,

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.380
so anyone can do it.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.050
I wonder what's wrong with vegetables lately.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.780
Maybe it's global warming?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.210
The skin is so thick, there's not much left inside.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.960
I wonder how many potatoes it 
takes just to make one portion.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:36.880
Huh?

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.560
Look, it's gotten so small...

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.340
<i>Okay, so maybe not just anyone.</i>

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.380
I wonder why...

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.130
Why am I crying so much?

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.510
That's what I want to know.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.010
My eyes... My eyes...

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:00.680
Kiryuu-senpai, should onions 
make people cry <i>this</i> much?

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.550
At home, we chill them before cutting them,

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.080
so they never make me cry this much.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:07.160
I've never cut this many at a time, either!

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.160
Here's a good trick.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.400
A good trick?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.040
If you hold a slice in your mouth while you cut,

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.580
you won't cry.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.360
Really?

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.560
Tell us that sooner!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.790
Let's try it.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.550
I feel so sad...

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.750
I'm tearing up even more now.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.970
Oh, dear... I'm sorry.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.570
It's not onion you put in your mouth.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:38.880
It's chopsticks.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.500
What?!

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.100
I guess I was a little off.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.500
Not just a little!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:49.900
Okay, I'll help out to make up for it.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.900
Here we go!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:52.880
Stop!

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.000
That's dangerous!

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.280
But if I uncover my eyes, I'll cry...

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.920
Watch it! Watch it!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.670
In those old movies, they tell 
you not to rely on your eyes,

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:03.500
but to know in your heart where to cut.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:12.920
Didn't it have a disclaimer saying 
the whole thing was fiction?

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.640
Did it?

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.080
Please work on something else, President.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.390
Risa-chan, help me.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:25.400
What's wrong, President?

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.030
I can't lift the pot.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:28.700
Huh?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.820
Let me see.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.260
This is heavy.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.690
What's in here?

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.530
It's full of water.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.670
I wanted to boil some water.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.320
If you're using a pot this big,

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.090
you put it on the stove first,

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.440
then put the water in with a bowl or hose.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.920
You know a lot, Risa-chan!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.960
Okay, I need to pour this water out, then.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.050
Risa-chan...

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:56.490
Let's take out the water little by little.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.550
I think our workload just got heavier.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.160
Sorry...

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.560
I appreciate it.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.060
I'm so tired.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:11.100
I feel more tired than I should, 
given the work we did.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.940
Good work.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.610
This milk tea is really sweet and delicious.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.600
I boiled the leaves in milk,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.330
and added some cream.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.220
It's rejuvenating, isn't it?

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.860
Yes, it would be perfect when you're tired.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:34.050
Everyone,

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:37.630
I'll do the rest of the cooking myself.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.570
Go and attend your classes.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.300
Okay.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.560
Meet back here again at lunch.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.220
Okay.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.400
I appreciate it, everyone.

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.180
Girl Friend BETA.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.370
Okay, we're going to open the cafeteria now.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.260
Everyone stay focused and do your best.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.040
Right!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.040
<b>Announcement 

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.750
They've got it running like any other day.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.400
Okay, then...

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.300
I'll take a kitsune udon and a katsu curry.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.230
A kitsune udon and a katsu curry...

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.040
That'll be 650 yen.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.550
You'll be number 20.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:23.180
Thank you for waiting.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.240
Stew, bread, coffee, and...

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:27.930
Natto?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.520
Um... Is this right?

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.870
Yes, of course.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:37.190
Countries with a long history 
have unique fermented foods.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.700
Natto is the soul of Japan.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.500
You're not going to mix that in, are you?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.750
Non, non.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:48.600
You have to stir the natto first.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:49.120
Huh?

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.160
You stir it well, without adding anything.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.270
That gives natto its aroma.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.530
When you're done stirring,

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.560
you add the sauce and spices.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.840
Everyone in Japan knows this.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.400
Right.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.100
<i>She did mix it in!</i>

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.010
Hey, do androids know what food tastes like?

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.930
Yes. Food tastes good.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:13.700
Is it some sort of chemical reaction?

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.940
Or is it the ions?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.570
Tell me how it works!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.860
That is classified.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.240
A meat and potatoes meal with a raw egg.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.400
Also, two AA batteries,

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:28.620
and one 006p 9V battery, please.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:32.360
AA batteries and a 9V battery...

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:35.130
That'll be 750 yen in total.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:38.290
We've got an order for curry and rice.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.130
Right!

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.810
Put some rice on the plate...

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:42.600
There.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.930
And then some curry...

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:46.700
There we are.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.850
I think that's a bit too much curry...

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.560
I'll just add some rice, then.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.320
There.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.510
Now there might be too much rice.

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.860
Then I'll just add more curry...

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:02.840
President Amatsu.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.610
Is the curry rea—

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.080
Don't look!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.400
Looking isn't the problem!

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.410
Are you angry?

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.910
No, I'm not.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.340
You are...

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:19.610
I'm not.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.340
I'm sorry.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.480
It's fine.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.090
Just go take orders.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.100
Okay!

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.090
Thanks for waiting.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:35.260
Meat and potatoes meal up!

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.330
Right!

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:38.640
Hey, Risa-chan.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.780
How do you cook teriyaki chicken steak?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.240
Huh?

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:45.990
We don't have teriyaki chicken 
steak on the menu today...

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.570
You didn't take an order for one, did you?

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.480
Yep!

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.720
Saya-chan said—

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:52.500
It doesn't matter what Saya-chan said!

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.620
Jeez... Why'd you take an order for 
something that's not on the menu?

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:59.310
No, I recommended it.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.040
I said it's really good.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.200
Give that to me.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.510
I'll do it.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.440
I appreciate it.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.180
The pace has slowed down.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.960
You should start taking breaks 
in shifts while you can.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:14.940
Right!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.150
I didn't think it'd be so tiring...

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.110
Yes, not to mention we have one girl

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.450
who's making things more 
tiring than they should be.

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:30.350
How did she even get to be 
the student council president?

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.620
Thank you!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.790
Good work.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.320
I wasn't sure how it'd turn out,

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.320
but I'm glad it worked out.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.260
I didn't think it would really go that well.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.010
You're the one who suggested this!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.520
Please work hard tomorrow, too.

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:51.640
Okay!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.090
Suzukawa-senpai, did you 
hear about the cafeteria?

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.660
Yep, I did.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:59.650
The student council's running it, right?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.570
My classmate went there to eat,

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.410
and the vice principal was directing them.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.260
Apparently, the food was pretty good.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.470
It's only for a limited time, right?

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.070
I'll have to give it a try, too!

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.330
The cafeteria?

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:18.160
I do recall them telling us to 
bring our lunches if we could...

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:23.340
Well, Amatsu-san wanted us to spread 
the word for everyone to come.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.590
The president did?

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:26.500
I'll go, then.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.470
I wanted to give it a try.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:33.720
<i>A stew suited to Japanese tastes 
that goes well with natto...</i>

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.160
<i>It was the best!</i>

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.480
<i>Give it a try.</i>

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:44.230
Isn't the line a little longer than yesterday?

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:48.740
You'd classify this as "a little," Mutsumi-chan?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.460
Oh, my.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.740
We're really in business now.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.040
It's not about being in business!

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.100
How are we going to deal 
with that many customers?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.630
I'm sure everyone's here because 
the food yesterday was so good.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.750
How nice.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.250
It's not nice at all!

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:05.950
Try your best.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:08.170
You're acting like you're not even involved...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.680
I'll try hard with you.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.360
Please, President, don't try at all.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:15.810
Vice President Shinomiya.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.970
We're definitely over capacity here.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.350
We have no choice, then.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.390
Ask the cooking club for help,

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:24.060
and get as many volunteers as you can!

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.570
<i>We've got a request from the student council!</i>

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.450
They're seeking students who 
can help out in the cafeteria.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.490
<i>Anyone who's good at cooking,</i>

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.200
<i>anyone who wants to be a waitress...</i>

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.570
<i>From cleaning to heavy lifting,</i>

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.710
<i>they'll gladly accept any help you can offer!</i>

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:45.710
<i>If you'd like to lend a hand, 
head to the cafeteria immediately!</i>

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.490
I'm Kaho Mishina, a first-year.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:52.090
I came here with Nabeshima-senpai to
 help on behalf of the cooking club.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.920
Otome Kayashima, a third-year.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:57.280
I'm in the Japanese culture research society,

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:59.230
but I'm pretty decent at cooking.

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:01.220
Makoto Hiiragi, a first-year.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.100
I like making sweets.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.370
Michiru Tomura, a second-year!

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.570
Leave the waitressing to me!

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.720
We have to work fast.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.760
Please start helping right away.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:12.820
Got it!

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.760
Welcome!

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.570
Help yourself to an open seat.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.920
Got an order for a tonkatsu meal.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:19.790
Okay!

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:23.960
Oh, you're great with a knife.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.130
The older club members have been teaching me.

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:29.240
Okay, one tonkatsu meal up!

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:30.630
I've got to try hard, too.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:34.340
The strawberry sundaes are done.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.360
They've got sweets today, too.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:40.680
Hey, what's this "Chef's Random Special"?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:42.310
It's random.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.850
I'm not sure what it is, either.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.730
We've got three Random Specials up.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.570
Character lunches?

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.740
Thanks for waiting.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:54.150
Huh?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.200
Suzukawa-senpai?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.930
Didn't you say you wanted to eat here?

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.700
When they said they needed 
the help, they weren't <i>kitten</i>.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.580
Well? How do I look <i>nyow</i>?

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:07.080
I guess we got to come...

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.990
But this isn't quite what I had in mind.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.590
This is a little embarrassing.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.510
Looks like everything's going smoothly.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.130
If we keep this up, I think we can make it.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.440
There's trouble, Vice President Shinomiya!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.020
What's wrong, Kiryuu-san?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:25.720
I just heard from a customer that

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.280
the school store messed up an order,

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.650
and didn't get any yakisoba bread in today.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.860
<b></b>We were unable to get any
yakisoba bread today. 
We apologize for
the inconvenience.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:35.070
All the people who were hoping to get 
yakisoba bread are going to come here.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.660
We're full over here.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.730
What should we do, Vice President?

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:41.490
I have a good idea.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:43.880
President Amatsu!

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.250
We just have to...

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.250
We just have to...?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.560
Make yakisoba bread ourselves!

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:51.250
What?!

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:54.160
We've got the bread,
and we've got the yakisoba.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:56.340
That solves the problem.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.900
No, it doesn't!

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:59.640
We still don't have enough people!

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:04.600
But don't you feel bad that people 
can't eat what they wanted to?

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.020
We're really busy as it is!

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.900
We can't add more menu items now!

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:10.880
Please...

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.960
Not happening.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:13.900
Please...

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.530
I said we can't.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:18.280
Please...

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:24.040
Pretty please?

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.040
We've got two orders for yakisoba bread!

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.830
Got it!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.670
Would you like me to help?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.900
No, thank you.

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:33.980
Really?

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:36.190
Don't do anything else.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.340
My hands are free, though.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.890
Go make some tea.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.370
Okay.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.580
Take breaks in shifts.

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:51.230
Shinomiya's going on her break.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.640
Huh? Where's President Amatsu?

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.780
Oh, well.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.800
I need to eat lunch while it's quiet,

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:00.740
and then get back.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.620
One Random Special.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.900
There, two curry udons up!

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:09.680
Vice President, we need three of those.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:11.350
Huh? We do?

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.540
Sorry. I'll make it now.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.430
Is the meat and potatoes meal ready yet?

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:17.760
Huh? Didn't I bring that out already?

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.420
That was the previous order.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.700
We got another one.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.820
Sorry, I'll make it now!

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:25.930
Vice President, what's that?

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:32.720
It was supposed to be curry and rice,
but now it's meat and potatoes with rice!

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.740
Is the vice president okay?

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.440
Should I switch with you?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.040
I can't do this anymore!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.160
Someone help me!

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.090
Okay!

00:19:58.570 --> 00:19:59.710
President?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.660
I'm back.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.090
I was out of tea.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.020
Here you go.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.400
It's good.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:19.200
I put honey in chamomile tea.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.490
It helps you calm down.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:22.710
Wow...

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.410
You're pretty amazing, Risa-chan.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.200
Huh?

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.250
We really were able to run the cafeteria.

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:29.910
That's because you suggested it.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:31.030
Yeah.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.060
All I did was say it.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:33.870
But, look...

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.380
Everyone's so happy.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.880
Seeing them all smiling makes me glad we did this.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:44.940
Don't you agree?

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.010
Is the tea good?

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:53.640
Yeah.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:55.600
I'm glad.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.600
President Amatsu.

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:58.890
What is it?

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:01.310
You're really terrible, aren't you?

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.170
Hm?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.310
I'm getting back to work.

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:11.540
See you later.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.410
Risa Shinomiya is in!

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:15.920
Right!

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:22.170
This is good.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.870
I'm tired.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:28.140
Here you go.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.860
What a refreshing smell.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.240
It's Darjeeling, first flush.

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:35.630
It helps refresh you.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.100
It brings me back to life.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:45.520
That was pretty fun, huh?

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:45.860
Yeah.

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:50.130
<i>I always end up following her lead...</i>

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:56.600
Everyone, good work.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:58.220
You, too.

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:00.330
I got word not too long ago.

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:02.400
The planes are able to fly now,

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:04.670
so the cafeteria staff will be heading back.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:06.850
So, tomorrow...

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:08.250
They won't be back yet.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:08.680
Huh?

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:10.480
From Easter Island,

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:12.720
they'll have to hit Santiago in Chile,

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:15.160
and then Paris, France,

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:17.350
and then from there to Narita.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:20.510
And then, they still have to head back here...

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:23.320
So they probably won't be back
tomorrow or even the day after.

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:24.400
What?

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.600
There you have it.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:28.240
So I'll be counting on you all tomorrow, too.

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:30.320
I guess there's no choice.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:34.120
I'll have to help out tomorrow, then.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:39.870
Please stay out of it!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:24.850
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:13.000
I'm Momoko Asahina. And...

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:14.550
Yuzuko Hazuki here.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:17.580
We're good friends, despite our opposing personalities.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:19.020
I appreciate your friendship.

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:20.140
You sure do.

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:22.560
Next time: Sweet Bitter Potato.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:24.850
<b>Episode 6: Sweet Bitter Potato</b>

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:24.850
This one's about us.
